From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:28:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/43] Shaders: fix v_div_fixup_f32 turning 0.0/x and x/Inf
 into +/-Infinity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In `Lower::valu` for `v_div_fixup_f32`, `q_nan` was ORed into `make_inf`
and applied after `make_zero`. Because `v_div_scale_f32` outputs `qNaN`
whenever either operand is zero (`0.0 / x`), and `v_fma_f32(-Inf, 0, 1)`
produces `qNaN` when the denominator is infinite (`x / +/-Inf`), both
`make_zero` and `q_nan` are true for those cases — causing `make_inf` to
overwrite `+/-0.0` with `+/-Infinity`.

Match the RDNA2/GFX10 `V_DIV_FIXUP_F32` priority order: apply
`q_nan -> signed_inf` below `make_zero` (`d_inf || n_zero`) so `0.0 / x`
and `x / +/-Inf` evaluate to signed zero while finite quotient overflow
(`q_nan` with finite non-zero inputs) still produces signed infinity.

Extend `valu_div_f32_sequence_executes_on_gpu` to test `0/1`, `-0/1`,
`0/-2`, `1/+Inf`, `-1/+Inf`, `+Inf/+Inf`, and `+/-1e38 / 1e-38` on both
hardware D3D12 and WARP.

(cherry picked from commit 84d0e6aead7660d963d1d39a5864823ec88daaaf)
(cherry picked from commit 441d3bb5c30ef5582b25f7f994ba7c7910d4fda1)
---
 crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs | 13 +++--
 crates/victory-shader/src/emit/mod.rs   | 72 +++++++++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 64 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs b/crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs
index 89d35964e..253ce2cd9 100644
--- a/crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs
+++ b/crates/victory-shader/src/emit/lower.rs
@@ -7207,16 +7207,19 @@ impl<'a> Lower<'a> {
                 let both_inf = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::And, n_inf, d_inf);
                 let both_zero = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::And, n_zero, d_zero);
                 let invalid = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, both_inf, both_zero);
-                let make_inf = {
-                    let t = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, n_inf, d_zero);
-                    self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, t, q_nan)
-                };
+                let make_inf = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, n_inf, d_zero);
                 let make_zero = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, d_inf, n_zero);
                 let signed_q = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, sign, q_abs);
                 let signed_inf = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, sign, kinf);
                 let n_qnan = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, ni, kqnan_bit);
                 let d_qnan = self.s.m.bin(c, Bin::Or, di, kqnan_bit);
-                let r = self.s.m.select(c, make_zero, sign, signed_q);
+                // Priority (highest to lowest): n_nan, d_nan, invalid (0/0 or
+                // Inf/Inf), make_inf (n_inf or d_zero), make_zero (d_inf or
+                // n_zero), q_nan (overflowed quotient -> signed Inf), signed_q.
+                // `q_nan` must stay below `make_zero` because `v_div_scale_f32`
+                // and `v_fma_f32(-Inf, 0, 1)` produce qNaN on `0 / x` and `x / Inf`.
+                let r = self.s.m.select(c, q_nan, signed_inf, signed_q);
+                let r = self.s.m.select(c, make_zero, sign, r);
                 let r = self.s.m.select(c, make_inf, signed_inf, r);
                 let r = self.s.m.select(c, invalid, kneg_qnan, r);
                 let r = self.s.m.select(c, d_nan, d_qnan, r);
